<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::diesel_supply_flow" target="china_taiwan_grayzone::coercion_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A fall in global diesel supply reduces available bunker and marine diesel for sustained PLA sorties and patrols, directly cutting the tempo and duration of naval and air shows of force around Taiwan (and conversely a supply increase enables higher sortie rates).</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">china_taiwan_grayzone</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::diesel_supply_flow" target="iran_houthi_maritime::seaborne_tanker_transit" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Loss of Russian diesel exports forces importers to source refined product from more distant suppliers (Middle East, East Asia), directly increasing the volume of tanker shipments transiting routes and chokepoints used by Iran-Houthi-affected maritime traffic.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
