<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::diesel_price_level" target="china_taiwan_grayzone::investor_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp diesel price increases raise logistics and manufacturing costs across East Asian supply chains, worsening near‑term earnings outlooks and volatility for firms exposed to cross‑strait trade and thereby increasing the investor risk premium on assets linked to Taiwan/China.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">china_taiwan_grayzone</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::diesel_price_level" target="eurozone_bond_stress::sovereign_credit_spreads" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in diesel prices raises near‑term inflation and fiscal outlays (via subsidies or weaker growth), deteriorating sovereign fiscal metrics and prompting investors to demand higher risk premia on eurozone sovereign debt.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">eurozone_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::diesel_price_level" target="iran_houthi_maritime::shipping_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher diesel prices raise the value of liquid cargoes and the economic payoff from interdiction or seizure, provoking insurers and charterers to demand larger risk premia for tankers operating in corridors vulnerable to Houthi action.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_houthi_maritime</data>
