  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Repeated upstream production shut‑ins increase energy-price volatility and highlight import vulnerability, prompting Chinese authorities to accelerate procurement and force-projection investments (naval logistics, escorts, stockpiles) to secure sea lines of supply.</data>
