  <data key="d36">Acute stress in eurozone banks contracts trade‑finance, reduces availability of letters of credit and counterparty capacity to back marine insurance/reinsurance, and thus forces insurers and charterers to charge higher premiums for tanker voyages through Houthi‑exposed routes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">eurozone_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_houthi_maritime</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eurozone_bond_stress::banking_sector_stress" target="russia_ukraine_war::diesel_supply_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Heightened bank stress leads banks to curtail trade finance, letters of credit and correspondent services used to finance and insure cross‑border fuel shipments, directly reducing the volume of diesel imports/exports that can be executed.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">eurozone_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eurozone_bond_stress::banking_sector_stress" target="us_china_ai_rivalry::compute_demand_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">When eurozone banking stress tightens lending to technology firms, many firms accelerate migration of AI training and inferencing to large US or Chinese cloud providers, increasing compute consumption intensity on those providers and concentrating demand in the US–China rivalry.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">eurozone_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_ai_rivalry</data>
</edge>
