<edge source="china_taiwan_grayzone::coercion_intensity" target="eurozone_bond_stress::market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute spikes in coercive military actions around Taiwan trigger immediate global risk repricing and surge in hedging activity, raising realized and implied volatility in eurozone fixed‑income and related derivatives markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_taiwan_grayzone</data>
  <data key="d39">eurozone_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_taiwan_grayzone::coercion_intensity" target="eurozone_bond_stress::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalation in gray‑zone coercion prompts a flight‑to‑quality that reallocates international portfolio flows into core eurozone sovereign bonds, increasing net inflows into euro area markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_taiwan_grayzone</data>
  <data key="d39">eurozone_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_taiwan_grayzone::coercion_intensity" target="iran_houthi_maritime::shipping_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in gray‑zone coercion around Taiwan forces redistribution of US/allied naval assets and raises insurer perceptions of correlated naval risk, prompting shipowners and insurers to reprice Middle East fuel routes and raise shipping premiums.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_taiwan_grayzone</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_houthi_maritime</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_taiwan_grayzone::coercion_intensity" target="iran_houthi_maritime::seaborne_tanker_transit" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained increases in coercive incidents drive shipping firms to avoid transits through chokepoints perceived as underprotected (e.g., Red Sea/Suez) because of reduced escort availability and tighter ROE, reducing tanker voyage frequency through those corridors.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_taiwan_grayzone</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_houthi_maritime</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_taiwan_grayzone::coercion_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::diesel_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalation of harassment and near‑shore military activity in the Taiwan Strait forces rerouting and delays for tankers and refined‑product shipments through key Asia hubs (Strait of Malacca/Singapore), raising freight and short‑term diesel scarcity that pushes up global diesel prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_taiwan_grayzone</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_taiwan_grayzone::coercion_intensity" target="us_china_ai_rivalry::compute_demand_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained gray‑zone coercion prompts US and allied defense and intelligence agencies to accelerate development and deployment of AI-enabled ISR, targeting, and wargaming models, increasing demand for high‑performance training and inference compute.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_taiwan_grayzone</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_ai_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_taiwan_grayzone::coercion_intensity" target="us_china_ai_rivalry::cyber_attack_activity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating maritime and air coercion triggers complementary hybrid operations (including offensive cyber and espionage) aimed at disrupting adversary command, AI data pipelines, and supporting infrastructure, raising the tempo of malicious cyber activity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_taiwan_grayzone</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_ai_rivalry</data>
</edge>
